92: - `D003`: convert D001 to the configured exchange IANA timezone without changing the instant.
93: - `D004`: obtain exchange-local trading date from the configured session calendar, including overnight/session boundary rules.
94: - `D005`: classify the local instant into an ordered, non-overlapping versioned session-phase schedule. A phase is absent if no configured phase contains the instant.
95: - `D009`: classify each visible macro vintage into one mutually exclusive category at the calculation knowledge cutoff: `initial` when it is the first published vintage; `latest_known_at_cutoff` when it is the newest visible non-initial vintage; otherwise `revised`. If only the initial vintage is visible, it remains `initial`. The occurrence also preserves the applicable vintage/realtime period and cutoff; `latest` is never a timeless claim.
96: - `D010`: true only when the configured market calendar says the instrument is open and the observation lies in the configured liquid/RTH phase; otherwise false when the state is knowable.
97: - `D062`: for the earliest relevant scheduled event strictly after the calculation as-of instant, return `{seconds=next_event_ts-as_of_ts, minutes=seconds/60}`; seconds is the canonical stored duration and minutes is an exact representation derived from it.
98: - `D085`: whole calendar-day difference between option expiry date and exchange-local trading date; negative values are invalid for a live contract calculation.
99: - `D086`: ACT/365F year fraction from D001 to the configured expiry instant. Expiry instant/session convention is versioned by instrument/calendar policy.
